+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Airbnb or a long-term rental more profitable in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"An Airbnb earns more once it books often enough. Run by its owner, a Myrtle Beach two-bedroom Airbnb keeps more than a yearly lease once it books about 82 nights a year at the area's average two-bedroom rate. At the top-quarter mark, run all year, an Airbnb keeps about $12,000 a year more than a lease."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you Airbnb a house in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not in most of the city's traditional neighborhoods. The City of Myrtle Beach allows stays under 90 days in no zoning district that begins with R, except RMV, the Residential Multifamily Visitor zone. We check the zoning on any address before you offer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many nights does a Myrtle Beach Airbnb need to book?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"About 82 a year to match a yearly lease on a two-bedroom, run by its owner: roughly 17 stays at the average length of 4.7 nights."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I pay lodging tax on a long-term lease?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No, not on a stay of 90 days or more. South Carolina charges a 7 percent state tax on a stay of under 90 days, plus local taxes. A tenant who stays 90 continuous days or more pays no lodging tax. Two exceptions to the tax: a home rented out 14 days or fewer in a year, and rooms in the owner's own home with fewer than six rented."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a short-term or long-term rental easier to finance?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A short-term rental meets two limits. A loan officer at our preferred lender tells us investor lenders count only about 75 percent of an Airbnb estimate, and standard Fannie Mae loans are not made in a condo project with a required rental pool or hotel services."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Chapter3 manage rentals?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Chapter3 is a brokerage and does not manage rentals. We run the address both ways and read the building's rules before you offer."}}]}</script>
