="rules" class="mg-section mg-col"> <div class="mg-title mb-8"> <p class="font-lato text-[12px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[rgba(0,0,0,0.6)]"> Permits </p> <h2 class="mg-serif mt-1.5 text-[30px] font-bold leading-[1.12] sm:text-[36px] tracking-[-0.012em] text-[#1e293b]"> Airbnb Permits and Registration in Myrtle Beach </h2>  </div> <div class="mg-report prose max-w-none"> <p id="rules-summary">Airbnb is legal in Myrtle Beach only in zones that allow rentals under 90 days, with a city business license; most residential neighborhoods are closed. Taxes total about 13% and Airbnb collects them.</p><div id="licensing-info"> <p id="licensing-info-summary">None of the 8,698 active listings in Myrtle Beach display a registration, permit or license number. That doesn't mean no rules apply: some places don't ask hosts to show a number on the listing, and listing data doesn't capture every scheme.</p> </div> <p>
